"hadiths[51]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1619,"Narrated Jabir bin ‘Abdullah : ""Umar bin Al-Khattab informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'I will expel the Jews and the Christians from the Arabian Peninsula"
1620,"Narrated Abu Hurairah: ""Fatimah came to Abu Bakr and said: 'Who will inherit from you?' He said: 'My family and my son.' She said: 'So what about me? I do not get inheritance from my father?' So Abu Bakr said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'We are not inherited from' but I support those whom the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to support"
1621,Narrated Abu Hurairah: That Fatimah came to Abu Bakr and 'Umar may Allah be pleased with them both
1622,"Narrated Malik bin Aws bin Al-Hadathan: ""I entered upon 'Umar bin Al-Khattab. (Then) Uthman bin 'Affan"
1623,"Narrated Al-Harith bin Malik bin Al-Barsa': ""On the day of the Conquest of Makkah"
1624,"Narrated An-Nu'man bin Muqarrin : ""I fought along with the Prophet (ﷺ)"
1625,"Narrated Ma'qil bin Yasar: ""Umar bin Al-Khattab sent An-Nu'man bin Muqarrin to Al-Hurmuzan."" And he mentioned the Hadith in its entirety. An-Nu'man bin Muqarrin said: ""I participated (in battles) with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). So when he did not fight in the beginning if the daytime"
1626,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""At-Tiyarah is from Shirk"
1627,"Narrated Anas: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no 'Adwa and no Tiyarah"
1628,"Narrated Anas bin Malik: That the Prophet (ﷺ) used to like it when he set out upon an affair if he heard: ""O directed one"
1629,"**Hadith Translation:**

It was narrated to us that Haddad narrated to us; Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Abd al-Malik bin 'Umair, from 'Atiyyah al-Qurazi, who said:

""We were presented before the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Qurayzah. Those among us who had signs of puberty (i.e., those upon whom hair had grown) were killed, and those who had not yet shown such signs were set free. I was among those who had not yet shown signs of puberty, so I was set free.""

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: *""This is a hasan sahih hadith.""*

**Scholarly Commentary:**

Abu 'Isa al-Tirmidhi further noted that this practice was adopted by certain scholars of the People of Knowledge, who considered the appearance of pubic hair (*al-inbat*) as an indicator of legal maturity (*bulugh*) when neither the age of the individual nor the experience of wet dreams (*ihtilam*) could be established. This was the position of Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ishaq ibn Rahawayh (may Allah have mercy upon them).

**Key Terms:**
- *Al-inbat* (الإنبات): The growth of coarse pubic hair, traditionally used as a physical marker of legal maturity (*bulugh*) in Islamic jurisprudence.
- *Bulugh* ("
1630,"he would exhort him concerning himself to have Taqwa of Allah, and he would exhort him to be good to those who are with him among the Muslims. He would say: 'Fight in the Name of Allah, in the cause of Allah. Fight those who disbelieve in Allah, and do not steal from the spoils of war or be treacherous, nor mutilate, and do not kill a child. When you meet your enemy among the idolaters, then call them to one of the three options or choices, whichever of them they respond to then accept it from them, and refrain from them. Call them to Islam, and to relocate from their land to the land of Emigrants. Inform them that if they do that, then they will have similar to what those who emigrated have, and from them will be required similar to what is required from those who have emigrated. And if they refuse to relocate, then inform them that they will be like the Bedouins among the Muslim, and they will be treated the same as Bedouins are treated. There is no war spoils or Fay' for them, unless they fight along with the Muslims. If they refuse then seek aid from Allah against them and fight them. And if you lay siege to a fortress and they want you to grant them covenant from Allah and a covenant of His Prophet, then do not grant them the covenant of Allah nor the covenant of His Prophet. Rather grant them your own covenant and the covenant of your companions, it will be better than breaking Allah's covenant and the covenant of His Messenger. And if you lay siege to the people of a fortress and they want you to lift the siege for negotiating upon the judgement of Allah, then do not stop, but rather make them surrender to your judgement, for you do not know if you will come upon the judgement of Allah regarding them or not.' Or similar to that. \n"
1631,"and the Hadith of Buraidah is a Hasan Sahih Hadith \nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1617 Arabic Hadees: 1617"""
1632,"Narrated to us Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated to us Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Bajalah, that 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used not to collect the jizyah from the Magians until 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had collected the jizyah from the Magians of Hajar. And in the hadith there is more speech than this. This is a hasan sahih hadith."
1633,"so if he heard the Adhan he would refrain, and if not, then he would attack. So he listened one day and heard a man saying: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, so he said: Upon the Fitrah. Then he said: I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah. So he said: You have departed from the Fire. \n\nAnother chain with similar narrations.\n\n[Abu 'Eisa said:\n\n] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. \nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1618 Arabic Hadees: 1618"""
1634,"# Hadith Translation

**Narrated by 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir (may Allah be pleased with him):**

He said: ""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we pass by a people who do not offer us hospitality, nor do they fulfil the rights that are due upon them towards us, and we do not take anything from them by force.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **'If they refuse [to offer anything] except that you take it by force, then take it.'**""

**Abu 'Isa [al-Tirmidhi] said:** This is a *hasan* (good) hadith. Al-Layth ibn Sa'd also narrated it from Yazid ibn Abi Habib. The meaning of this hadith, as explained, is that they used to go out on military expeditions and pass by a people from whom they could not find food to purchase at a price. So the Prophet ﷺ said: **'If they refuse to sell except that you take it by force, then take it.'** Thus it has been narrated in some reports with explanation. And it has also been narrated from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to command something similar to this.

---

*— Extracted from Sunan al-Tirmidhi*"
1635,"Narrated Anas bin Malik: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: meaning: Allah Mighty and Sublime is He says: 'The Mujahid in My cause"
1636,"Narrated Fadalah bin 'Ubaid: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The deeds of everyone who dies are sealed. Except for the one who dies guarding the frontier from the enemy"
1637,"Qutaybah narrated to us that Hatim bin Isma'il narrated to us from Yazid bin Abi Ubayd, who said: I asked Salamah bin Al-Akwa', ""On what did you pledge to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the day of Al-Hudaybiyyah?"" He replied, ""On death."" This is a hasan sahih hadith."
1638,"Narrated Abu Sa’id Al Khudri : That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""A worshipper does not fast a day in the cause of Allah except that"
1639,"Narrated by Ahmad ibn Mani', narrated by Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""We did not pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to die; rather, we pledged allegiance to him that we would not flee."" Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This hadith is hasan sahih. The meaning of both hadiths is correct. Some of his Companions pledged allegiance to him to die, saying, ""We will remain before you until we are killed,"" while others pledged allegiance, saying, ""We will not flee."""
1640,"Narrated Khuraim bin Fatik: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever spends a sum in the cause of Allah"
1641,Narrated 'Adi bin Hatim At-Tai: That he asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)
1642,"Narrated Abu Umamah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The most virtuous of charitable spending is the shade of a tent in the cause of Allah"
1643,Narrated Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said
1644,Narrated Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said
1645,Narrated Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said similarly
1646,Narrated Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said
1647,"Narrated Yazid bin Abu Maryam: ""Abayah bin Rifa'ah bin Rafi' met me while I was walking to the Friday prayer. He said: 'Have glad tidings"
1648,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Qutaybah, who narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad, from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:**

**""Do not initiate the greeting of *salām* upon the Jews and the Christians. And if you encounter any one of them on the road, then compel them to its narrowest part.""**

He (the compiler) said: **""In this chapter (there are narrations) from Ibn ʿUmar, Anas, and Abū Baṣrah al-Ghifārī, a Companion of the Prophet ﷺ.""**

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **""This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* Hadith.""**

**The meaning of this Hadith — ""Do not initiate the greeting of *salām* upon the Jews and the Christians""** — is explained by some of the people of knowledge as follows: **""The reason for the dislike (of initiating the greeting) is that it constitutes a form of honouring them. Rather, the Muslims have been commanded to humiliate them. Likewise, if one encounters any of them on the road, he should not leave the path for them, for that too constitutes a form of honouring them.""**

---

*This Hadith is recorded in Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim and Jāmiʿ al-Tirmidhī, and it pertains to the rulings governing interactions with the People of the Book (Ahl al-Kitāb) in matters of greeting and conduct on public pathways.*"
1649,"Narrated Shurahbil bin As-Samt: ""O Ka'b bin Murrah! Relate (something) to is from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
1650,"Narrated Amr bin 'Abasah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever develops some gray hair in the cause of Allah"
1651,"Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The forelocks of horses contain good until the Day of Judgement. The horse is for three (purposes): It is for one man a reward"
1652,"Narrated Abu Najih As-Sulami: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: ""Whoever shoots an arrow in the cause of Allah"
1653,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying"
1654,"Narrated Anas: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Dying in the cause of Allah expiates every sin."" Jibril said: ""Except for debt."" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Except the debt."" [Abu 'Eisa said:] There are narrations on this topic from Ka'b bin 'Ujrah"
1655,"Narrated Ka'b bin Malik: From his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The souls of the martyrs are in green birds"
1656,"# Translation of the Hadith

Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallāl narrated to us, that Bishr ibn ʿUmar informed us, that Mālik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Mālik ibn Aws ibn al-Ḥadathān, who said:

I entered upon ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, and ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, and Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ entered upon him. Then ʿAlī and al-ʿAbbās came, disputing with one another. So ʿUmar said to them:

""I adjure you by Allah, by whose command the heavens and the earth stand — do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **'We do not leave inheritance; whatever we leave is charity (ṣadaqah).'**""

They said: ""Yes.""

ʿUmar said: ""When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, Abū Bakr said: 'I am the successor (walī) of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So you and this one (meaning ʿAlī and al-ʿAbbās) came to Abū Bakr — you seeking your inheritance from your nephew, and this one seeking the inheritance of his wife from her father. So Abū Bakr said: 'Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **""We do not leave inheritance; whatever we leave is charity (ṣadaqah).""** And Allah knows that he (the Prophet ﷺ) was truthful, righteous, rightly guided, and a follower of the truth.'""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""And in the Hadith there is a long story.""

And this is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ gharīb* Hadith from the narration of Mālik ibn Anas (may Allah be pleased with them all)."
1657,"Narrated by Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated by Yahya ibn Sa'id, narrated by Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith ibn Malik ibn al-Barsa', who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, on the day of the conquest of Makkah, say: ""This city shall not be fought over after this day until the Day of Judgment."" Abu Isa said: In this chapter, there are narrations from Ibn Abbas, Sulayman ibn Surad, and Mu'ti'. This is a hasan sahith hadith, and it is the hadith of Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah from al-Sha'bi; we do not know it except from his narration."
1658,"Narrated Fadalah bin 'Ubaid: That he heard 'Umar bin Al-Khattab saying: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'The martyrs are four: A believing man whose faith is good"
1659,"Narrated Ishaq bin 'Abdullah bin Abi Talhah: That he heard Anas [bin Malik] saying: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to visit Umm Haram bint Milhan"
1660,"Narrated Abu Musa: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about a man who fights out of bravery"
1661,"Narrated 'Umar bin Al-Khattab: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Deeds are but with intentions"
1662,"Narrated Sahl bin Sa'd As-Sa'idi: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Going out in the morning in the cause of Allah is better that the world and what is in it. And the place (the size) of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."" [Abu 'Eisa said:] There are narrations on this topic from Abu Hurairah"
1663,"Narrated Abu Hurairah and Ibn 'Abbas: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Going out in the morning in the cause of Allah"
1664,Narrated Abu Hurairah: A man from the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) passed by ravine containing a small spring of thirst quenching water
1665,"Narrated Anas: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""To go out in the cause of Allah in the morning"
1666,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Shall I not inform you of the best of the people ? A man who takes hold of the reins of his horse in Allah's cause. Shall I not inform you of the one who comes after him ? The man who secludes himself from the people with a small group of sheep of his"
1667,"Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever meets Allah without any traces from Jihad he meets Allah with a defect. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Gharib as a narration of Al-Walid bin Muslim from Isma'il bin Rafi'. Isma'il bin Rafi' was graded weak by some of the people of Hadith. I heard Muhammad saying: ""He is trustworthy"
1668,"Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazee', narrated to us Al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman, narrated to me Marzooq Abu Bakr, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said — meaning, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: ""The one who strives in the cause of Allah is under My guarantee. If I take his soul, I shall grant him Paradise, and if I return him, I shall return him with reward or spoils of war."" He (the narrator) said: ""It is sahih (authentic) and gharib (uncommon) from this chain of narration."""
1669,"Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The martyr does not sense the touch of death except as one of you senses the touch of a (bug) bite. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Gharib Sahih"
